WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.090
The Truth Machine by Norman Whitney, a Heinemann guided reader at beginner level.

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:28.070
Copyright Heinemann International, first recorded 1982, this edition 1992.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.590
Chapter 1 Success for Professor Verity

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:36.830
Success, cried Professor Verity.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.990
My new invention is ready.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.950
It is now complete.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.710
I shall call it the Truth Machine.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.870
The professor ran to the telephone and phoned the newspaper office.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:51.560
He told them about the Truth Machine.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:55.750
Come to my laboratory, he said.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.470
You will see my new invention.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.910
I call it the Truth Machine.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:07.310
Please give us your name and address, said the girl at the newspaper office.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.270
We'll send a reporter immediately.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:15.790
The professor gave the girl his name and address.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.630
Will the reporter be here soon, he asked?

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.350
Yes, of course, replied the girl.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.590
Good, said Professor Verity.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.750
He smiled, he waited.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:33.710
The reporter soon arrived at the laboratory.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.590
Who can use the Truth Machine, Professor?

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.030
He asked.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:42.230
Anybody can use it, replied Professor Verity.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.870
But how does the machine work?

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.750
Asked the reporter.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.630
The professor laughed.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:51.710
That's the secret, he said.

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:53.910
But I can tell you this.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:58.910
The questioner sits in the little chair, eyes sit at the controls,

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.110
and the Truth speaker sits in the big chair.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:05.710
The Truth speaker always speaks the truth.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.350
He cannot tell lies.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.710
The professor smiled.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:13.310
Why did you make the Truth Machine?

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.470
Asked the reporter.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:20.830
I love Truth, said Professor Verity, and I hate lies.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.670
I love good people, and I hate bad people.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.950
I love peace, and I hate war.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.710
The Truth Machine loves Truth, good people, and peace.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:36.630
It hates lies, bad people, and war.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:40.470
The reporter wrote all this in his notebook.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:45.270
Soon everybody will know about the Truth Machine, said the professor.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:48.190
It will be a success.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:55.550
The reporter thanked the professor, and hurried back to his newspaper office.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.670
Professor Verity was right.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:02.470
Soon millions of people knew about the Truth Machine.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.630
The professor was on the radio.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.070
He was on the television, too.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:13.030
All over the world, newspapers and magazines wrote about Professor Verity and the Truth

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.070
Machine.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.950
Many people wrote to Professor Verity.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:24.510
Rich people, poor people, young people, old people, everybody sent letters.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.230
The Truth Machine was a success.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:31.190
Thank you, wrote one woman.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:34.190
Wonderful, wrote another.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:36.630
Good luck, wrote one man.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:38.550
I am sending you some money.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:41.070
It will help your work.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.230
Many people sent money.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:51.910
Some sent coins, others sent banknotes, and others sent checks and money orders.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.630
Then the professor chose his first clients.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.630
He read his letters many times.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:00.990
First, he chose a hundred letters.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.430
Then he chose fifty of them.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.990
Then he chose ten names.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:09.870
Finally, he chose three people.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:17.230
This is Seeker from Australia, Inspector Sack from South America, and Dr. Simple from

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.430
the United States.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:25.630
Professor Verity wrote to them, Please come and see me, he wrote.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.920
You will be one of my first clients.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:44.990
Chapter 2.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:49.470
Three visitors for Professor Verity.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:53.310
Two weeks later, Professor Verity had a visitor.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.230
It was Mrs. Seeker.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:57.150
She was from Australia.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.230
She was a housewife.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.710
She was afraid.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:04.030
Can I help you, Mrs. Seeker?

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.590
Ask the professor.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:08.560
Yes, Mrs. Seeker replied.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.950
I wrote to you about the truth machine.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.430
I know, said the professor.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.550
You will be my first client.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.470
Don't be afraid.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:20.710
Oh, said Mrs. Seeker.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:23.590
I will not be your first client, Professor.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:26.870
Your first client will be my husband.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:30.110
Your husband, said Professor Verity.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.510
The professor was surprised.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:35.560
But your husband didn't write to me.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:38.950
No, he didn't, said Mrs. Seeker.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.310
I wrote to you.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.990
But what do you want?

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:44.510
Ask the professor.

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.950
Why are you here?

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.910
Well, said Mrs. Seeker.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:53.430
My husband, Mrs. Seeker, stopped.

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:54.790
She was crying.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:56.910
She was unhappy.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.830
My husband as Mrs. Seeker stopped again.

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.550
She was crying again.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:07.110
Oh, said the professor quietly.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:11.550
Your husband has another woman.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.630
Yes, yes.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:15.350
Pride, Mrs. Seeker.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.150
But I don't know.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.950
Oh, I hate lies.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.950
I want the truth, Professor.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:25.230
I want the truth from my husband.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.950
But will he come here?

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.870
Ask the professor.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.950
Oh, yes, he'll come.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.070
Said Mrs. Seeker.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.630
Well, bring him to my laboratory, said the professor.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:39.830
I'll help you, Mrs. Seeker.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:43.950
Of course, there will be a small charge, a fee.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.190
I'll pay anything, said Mrs. Seeker.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.710
I hate lies.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.710
I want the truth from my husband.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:55.510
Come here next Monday morning, said the professor.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:59.030
Everything will be ready.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:02.070
The next visitor was Inspector Sack.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:04.270
He was from South America.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:07.670
He was a policeman, and he had a gun.

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.670
Hello, Professor!

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:11.510
Said the inspector.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:15.150
The inspector had a loud voice.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.070
Where is it, Professor?

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.230
He shouted.

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:21.670
Where is the truth machine?

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:26.350
It's here, Inspector, said Professor Verity quietly.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:29.440
You will be one of my first clients.

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:33.670
All good, said the inspector.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.550
Inspector Sack walked up and down.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.030
Then he stopped.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:40.510
He looked at the professor.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.430
Crime, shouted Inspector Sack.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:47.430
Crime, crime, crime.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:51.190
Crime, asked the professor in a soft voice.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:55.230
Yes, crime, shouted Inspector Sack.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.350
I hate criminals.

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:59.710
Murderers are criminals.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:01.550
They kill people.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.910
I hate murderers.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:06.030
Thieves are criminals.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:08.390
They take things from people.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.550
I hate thieves.

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:13.350
And liars are criminals.

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.350
They tell lies.

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:18.270
I hate lies, Professor.

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:21.910
I hate all criminals.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:28.030
But the truth machine will fight criminals, said Professor Verity quietly.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:30.910
There will be no more murderers and thieves.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:35.750
There will be no more lies and no more crime, Inspector.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:41.630
No more criminals and no more crime, shouted Inspector Sack.

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.230
Excellent.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:48.470
Bring your criminals to me, Inspector, said the professor.

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:52.550
Of course, there will be a small charge, a fee.

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:53.670
Money?

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:55.590
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:58.270
You shall have money, Professor.

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:00.870
We are fighting crime, my friend.

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:04.550
Of course, you shall have money.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:08.230
Thank you, Inspector, said Professor Verity.

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:09.950
Thank you.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:12.510
Come here next Monday afternoon.

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:14.830
Bring your criminals to me.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:15.960
Everything will be ready.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.630
Good morning, Professor Verity.

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:24.470
My name is Dr. Simple.

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:27.310
Dr. Simple was the third visitor.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:29.590
He was from the United States.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:31.590
He was a government official.

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:34.670
He worked for the American government.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:38.190
Hello, Dr. Simple, said the professor.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:41.270
You will be one of my first clients.

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:43.990
I know, said Dr. Simple.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:46.390
I will be your third client.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:50.870
The other two are Mrs. Seeker and Inspector Sack.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:53.470
Hello, said the professor.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:56.030
How do you know their names?

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:58.870
Dr. Simple looked round.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:04.030
Spies, Professor Verity, said Dr. Simple quietly.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.150
Spies.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:09.470
Spies, asked Professor Verity.

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:13.710
But Mrs. Seeker and Inspector Sack aren't spies.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:18.150
Of course, they are not spies, said Dr. Simple.

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:19.830
He looked round.

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:22.630
But I am.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:27.270
Oh, you are a spy, the professor asked.

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:30.190
Yes, said Dr. Simple.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:32.550
I'm a spy.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:33.910
He looked round.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:37.070
He was looking for enemy spies.

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:40.990
I fight for peace, said Dr. Simple.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.310
Professor Verity is smiled.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:47.510
Oh, I want peace too, the professor said.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.270
I know, said Dr. Simple.

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:51.750
He smiled.

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:53.870
You will help me, Professor.

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:56.390
We have caught an enemy spy.

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:58.510
He will not tell the truth.

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:00.430
I will bring him here.

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:02.070
I will be the questioner.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.950
He will be the truth speaker.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.070
Yes, said the professor.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:09.150
Please bring him here.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:13.910
Of course, Dr. Simple, there will be a small charge, a fee.

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:15.870
Dr. Simple smiled.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:17.950
He looked round again.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:21.790
Of course, Professor, here is some money.

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:25.790
Dr. Simple gave the professor a lot of money.

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:29.110
Thank you, said the professor quietly.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:31.310
He looked round too.

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:34.550
Come here with your spy next Monday evening.

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:36.550
Everything will be ready.

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:53.190
CHAPTER 3

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:58.190
MONDAY A BUSY DAY FOR PROFESSOR Verity

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:00.150
It was Monday morning.

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:02.870
Mrs. Seeker came to the laboratory.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:04.920
Mr. Seeker came too.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:07.070
How are you, Professor?

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:08.750
Said Mr. Seeker.

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:12.790
Where is your truth, machine?

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:14.790
Mr. Seeker laughed.

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:17.870
Don't laugh, said his wife.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.470
She was afraid.

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:21.910
Listen to the professor.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:24.630
Professor Verity spoke.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:27.830
Mrs. Seeker, you are the questioner.

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:30.110
Sit in the small chair.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:33.350
Mr. Seeker, you are the truth speaker.

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:36.310
Sit in the big chair.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:39.550
Mr. and Mrs. Seeker sat in their chairs.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:42.830
Mrs. Seeker looked at the professor.

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:44.590
What shall I say?

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:46.390
She asked.

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:51.150
Ask your husband some easy questions, said the professor.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:53.950
She looked at her husband.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.750
What is your name?

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:57.270
She asked.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:13:00.710
My name is Henry, said her husband.

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:03.310
That was an easy question.

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:05.270
He laughed.

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:07.670
How old are you, Henry?

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.590
Asked Mrs. Seeker.

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:16.430
I'm 47, said Mr. Seeker.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.150
Mrs. Seeker looked at Professor Verity.

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:20.750
She smiled.

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.190
That's the truth, she said.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:26.800
He usually says 43.

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:28.400
My husband is telling the truth.

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:34.750
Good, said Professor Verity.

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:39.030
Now ask your husband some difficult questions.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:43.710
Mrs. Seeker was afraid, but she spoke.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.470
Are you married?

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:46.950
She asked.

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:48.790
Of course I'm married.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:50.550
Replied, Mr. Seeker.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:52.430
You're my wife.

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:54.390
He was angry.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:58.910
But do you love me?

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:01.150
Asked Mrs. Seeker.

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:03.950
Mr. Seeker looked at his wife.

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:06.550
She waited.

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:10.270
Now, he said slowly.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:13.350
Now, I don't love you.

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:16.230
I'll have another woman.

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:19.150
Oh, said Mrs. Seeker.

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:20.790
Who do you love?

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:21.990
Tell me the truth.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.270
I hate lies.

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:25.270
Who do you love?

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:27.790
Mrs. Seeker was crying.

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:31.030
Mr. Seeker looked at his wife.

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:33.590
I love anelyate.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:38.070
I love anelyate, he said.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:41.030
Oh, anelyate.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:44.030
But she's my best friend.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:46.790
Now you know the truth.

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:50.390
Yes, that's the truth.

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:57.390
What shall I do now?

00:14:57.440 --> 00:15:01.670
Inspector Sack came to the laboratory on Monday afternoon.

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:05.030
His boss, the chief inspector, came too.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:08.990
They brought some criminals with them.

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:11.190
Good afternoon, professor.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:13.310
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:16.310
This is my boss, the chief inspector.

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:18.470
And these are the criminals.

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.190
They are murderers.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:21.710
They are thieves.

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:24.310
And they are liars.

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:30.070
But today, said Professor Verity, they will tell the truth.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:31.710
Shall we begin?

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:34.990
Said the chief inspector quietly.

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:36.830
Yes, let's begin.

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:37.990
Come on.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.270
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:43.550
Inspector Sack sat in the questioner's chair.

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:47.150
The first criminal sat in the truth speaker's chair.

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:49.470
Inspector Sack spoke.

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:53.990
Did you take money from the car of Senor Cavallio?

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:55.710
He asked.

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:58.630
Yes, I took the money.

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:00.270
Said the criminal.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:01.430
Guilty.

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:03.390
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:05.710
Five years in prison.

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:07.910
Next criminal.

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:11.990
The next criminal sat in the truth speaker's chair.

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:17.030
Did you take diamonds from the house of Senorita Regia?

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:19.390
Asked Inspector Sack.

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:21.430
Yes, I did.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:23.030
Said the criminal.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:24.070
Guilty.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:25.790
Shouted the inspector.

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:28.110
Ten years in prison.

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.080
Next criminal.

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:34.630
The next criminal came in.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:37.870
He sat in the truth speaker's chair.

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:41.350
Did you kill Senor Regia?

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:43.830
Asked Inspector Sack.

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:46.310
The criminal was silent.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:48.550
Then he spoke.

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:50.910
Yes, I did.

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:52.910
He said.

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:54.910
That was the truth.

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:56.030
Guilty.

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:57.910
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:59.790
Twenty years.

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:01.630
Next.

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:04.830
All the criminals sat in the truth speaker's chair.

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:07.030
They all told the truth.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:09.550
One of them was innocent.

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:11.750
You are not guilty.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:13.390
Said Inspector Sack.

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:16.190
You can go home.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:18.430
Inspector Sack was pleased.

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:20.710
Professor Verity was pleased.

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:22.990
The Chief Inspector was pleased.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:25.230
Good work, Sack.

00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:27.150
Said the Chief Inspector.

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:29.070
Very good work.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:30.990
Thank you, sir.

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:32.790
Said Inspector Sack.

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:35.110
We are fighting crime, sir.

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:37.710
The throat machine is helping us.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:42.110
There are no more criminals for us, sir.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.750
Inspector Sack smiled.

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:45.390
He was happy.

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:48.150
Yes, Inspector Sack.

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:50.150
No more criminals.

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:52.950
No more work.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:56.190
No more work for me, sir.

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:57.350
Yes.

00:17:57.400 --> 00:18:00.710
We don't need you now, Inspector Sack.

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:03.070
I haven't got a job.

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:08.910
What shall I do now?

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:10.950
It was Monday evening.

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:14.110
Doctor Simple came to the laboratory.

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:16.070
Another man came with him.

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:18.070
The other man was a spy.

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:20.790
Good evening, Professor.

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:22.790
Said Doctor Simple.

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:24.630
Good evening, Doctor Simple.

00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:26.470
Said the Professor.

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:28.030
Everything is ready.

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:31.030
Good, said Doctor Simple.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:33.270
This spy is dangerous.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:34.870
He is an enemy.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:36.790
I will be his questioner.

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:38.950
He will be the truth speaker.

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:41.790
He will tell the truth.

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:44.230
The Professor went to the controls.

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:47.030
Doctor Simple sat in the questioner's chair.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:50.550
The spy sat in the truth speaker's chair.

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:52.150
What is your name?

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:54.310
Asked Doctor Simple.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:57.190
My name is Horaville Wein.

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:59.190
Said the spy.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:00.870
Where are you from?

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:02.790
Asked Doctor Simple.

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:04.950
I am from Russia.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.710
Said the spy.

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:08.710
The spy smiled.

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:11.190
Doctor Simple looked at the Professor.

00:19:11.240 --> 00:19:13.670
Doctor Simple was pleased.

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:15.750
Excellent, Professor Verity.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:17.590
Said Doctor Simple.

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:19.430
Lime is telling the truth.

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:22.470
He will tell me everything.

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:24.120
Professor Verity was happy.

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:28.680
Doctor Simple looked at Lime.

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:31.240
Are you a spy?

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:32.600
He asked.

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:36.040
Yes, I am a spy.

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:38.600
I am an important spy.

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:39.880
Said Lime.

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:44.520
Do you know the secret of the new military aircraft?

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:45.800
He asked.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:48.360
How the lime smiled.

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:50.920
Yes, he said.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:55.830
I know the secret of the new military aircraft.

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:57.720
And my government knows too.

00:19:59.080 --> 00:19:59.400
Ahh!

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:01.750
Cried Doctor Simple.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:04.310
The truth machine is wonderful.

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:06.440
The spy is telling me everything.

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:09.480
But I have another secret.

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:10.840
Said Lime.

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:13.080
He looked at Doctor Simple.

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:15.480
He looked at Professor Verity.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:17.990
Another secret.

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:19.430
Cried Doctor Simple.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:21.720
Tell me, tell me, tell me the truth.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:24.760
My secret is this.

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:26.600
Said Harvey Lime.

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:29.240
I never tell the truth.

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:31.720
I always tell lies.

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:33.480
He smiled.

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:36.280
What do you mean?

00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:39.080
That's the truth.

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:40.840
I always tell lies.

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:45.080
Is Lime telling the truth?

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:47.400
Or is he lying?

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:11.080
What do you mean?

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:13.800
Chapter 4.

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:15.400
Tuesday.

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:17.080
An important meeting.

00:21:18.680 --> 00:21:20.680
There was a hotel near the laboratory.

00:21:21.560 --> 00:21:23.080
Mrs. Seeker was staying there.

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:27.160
Inspector Sack and Doctor Simple were staying there too.

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:33.160
Mrs. Seeker, Inspector Sack and Doctor Simple were eating breakfast together.

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:36.600
I know the truth about my husband.

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:39.080
Now I am very unhappy.

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:40.840
Said Mrs. Seeker.

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:44.760
I know the truth about my criminals.

00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:47.320
Now I haven't got a job.

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:49.160
Said Inspector Sack.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:52.440
I know the truth about my spy.

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:54.520
What shall I do now?

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:56.120
Said Doctor Simple.

00:21:57.640 --> 00:21:59.080
Mrs. Seeker was crying.

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:02.440
I don't like the truth, machine.

00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:03.000
She said.

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:07.000
Inspector Sack and Doctor Simple agreed with her.

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:10.520
Inspector Sack shouted in a loud voice.

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:14.440
We paid the professor a lot of money.

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:15.480
He said.

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:19.240
Mrs. Seeker and Doctor Simple agreed with him.

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:23.080
Doctor Simple spoke quietly and slowly.

00:22:24.520 --> 00:22:27.160
Professor Verity is a criminal.

00:22:27.800 --> 00:22:28.280
He said.

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:32.360
Mrs. Seeker and Inspector Sack agreed with him.

00:22:33.320 --> 00:22:35.480
I'm going to say Professor Verity.

00:22:35.880 --> 00:22:36.920
Said Mrs. Seeker.

00:22:37.640 --> 00:22:39.080
I shall come with you.

00:22:39.640 --> 00:22:41.000
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:43.640
A good idea.

00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:45.960
Said Doctor Simple slowly.

00:22:46.760 --> 00:22:47.960
I shall come too.

00:22:49.640 --> 00:22:53.880
Mrs. Seeker, Inspector Sack and Doctor Simple left the hotel.

00:22:54.680 --> 00:22:56.520
They wanted to see Professor Verity.

00:22:57.400 --> 00:22:58.680
They went to the laboratory.

00:23:02.440 --> 00:23:04.440
I shall come with you.

00:23:12.440 --> 00:23:13.320
Chapter 5.

00:23:14.280 --> 00:23:15.640
At the laboratory again.

00:23:17.400 --> 00:23:22.520
Soon Mrs. Seeker, Inspector Sack and Doctor Simple were at the laboratory.

00:23:23.640 --> 00:23:26.280
Oh, I hate you, Professor Verity.

00:23:27.080 --> 00:23:28.200
Cried Mrs. Seeker.

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:31.240
I want my money back, Professor.

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:33.000
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:35.480
You're a criminal, Verity.

00:23:36.120 --> 00:23:37.160
Said Doctor Simple.

00:23:38.600 --> 00:23:41.480
Professor Verity looked at his first three clients.

00:23:42.920 --> 00:23:44.600
Fools, he said.

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:46.600
You are fools.

00:23:47.240 --> 00:23:48.710
You wanted the truth.

00:23:48.760 --> 00:23:50.470
I gave you the truth.

00:23:50.520 --> 00:23:53.000
The truth machine gave you the truth.

00:23:53.960 --> 00:23:54.360
Truth?

00:23:54.920 --> 00:23:56.310
Said Mrs. Seeker.

00:23:56.360 --> 00:23:57.960
But now I am unhappy.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:23:59.560
Throws?

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:01.910
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:04.040
But now I haven't got a job.

00:24:05.560 --> 00:24:06.040
Truth?

00:24:06.600 --> 00:24:07.560
Said Doctor Simple.

00:24:08.120 --> 00:24:09.480
But what is the truth?

00:24:10.920 --> 00:24:12.040
What is the truth?

00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:13.800
Said Professor Verity.

00:24:14.520 --> 00:24:15.480
Let me tell you.

00:24:16.280 --> 00:24:20.150
Mrs. Seeker, you hate lies and I gave you the truth.

00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:22.310
Your husband loves Anne Elliot.

00:24:22.360 --> 00:24:23.400
That is the truth.

00:24:24.120 --> 00:24:26.790
Inspector, the professor went on.

00:24:26.840 --> 00:24:28.310
You hate crime.

00:24:28.360 --> 00:24:30.550
I put your criminals in prison.

00:24:30.600 --> 00:24:31.720
That is the truth.

00:24:32.680 --> 00:24:33.510
Simple.

00:24:33.560 --> 00:24:34.440
Said the professor.

00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:36.120
You fight for peace.

00:24:36.760 --> 00:24:37.990
I helped you.

00:24:38.040 --> 00:24:39.320
That is the truth.

00:24:40.600 --> 00:24:41.800
The professor stopped.

00:24:42.440 --> 00:24:43.480
Then he spoke again.

00:24:44.760 --> 00:24:46.360
Fools, he said.

00:24:47.080 --> 00:24:47.880
Go home.

00:24:49.320 --> 00:24:52.200
Do you really hate lies, Professor Verity?

00:24:52.920 --> 00:24:53.960
Asked Mrs. Seeker.

00:24:54.840 --> 00:24:57.480
Do you really hate crime, Professor?

00:24:58.120 --> 00:24:59.400
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:25:00.120 --> 00:25:02.040
And do you really fight for peace?

00:25:02.760 --> 00:25:03.800
Asked Doctor Simple.

00:25:04.680 --> 00:25:06.360
Yes, yes, yes.

00:25:06.920 --> 00:25:08.390
Cried Professor Verity.

00:25:08.440 --> 00:25:09.320
That's the truth.

00:25:10.840 --> 00:25:12.280
Then Doctor Simple spoke.

00:25:13.640 --> 00:25:14.600
We shall see.

00:25:15.400 --> 00:25:15.880
He said.

00:25:16.840 --> 00:25:19.720
Professor Verity will be the truth speaker.

00:25:24.440 --> 00:25:26.760
Why did you invent the truth machine?

00:25:28.280 --> 00:25:28.840
Success.

00:25:29.720 --> 00:25:30.680
I want success.

00:25:32.120 --> 00:25:33.800
What do you really want?

00:25:35.560 --> 00:25:35.880
Money.

00:25:36.680 --> 00:25:37.400
I want money.

00:25:39.000 --> 00:25:40.680
What do you really want?

00:25:42.360 --> 00:25:42.680
Power.

00:25:43.640 --> 00:25:44.440
I want power.

00:25:45.640 --> 00:25:48.310
You don't hate lies, Professor Verity.

00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:49.480
You want success?

00:25:50.360 --> 00:25:51.320
Said Mrs. Seeker.

00:25:52.200 --> 00:25:54.550
You don't hate crime, Professor.

00:25:54.600 --> 00:25:56.200
You want money.

00:25:56.840 --> 00:25:58.120
Shouted Inspector Sack.

00:25:58.920 --> 00:26:00.680
You don't want peace, Verity.

00:26:01.160 --> 00:26:02.280
You want power.

00:26:02.840 --> 00:26:03.880
Said Doctor Simple.

00:26:04.760 --> 00:26:05.080
Yes.

00:26:05.880 --> 00:26:07.080
Laugh, Professor Verity.

00:26:07.880 --> 00:26:09.000
You fools.

00:26:09.560 --> 00:26:11.080
You gave me success.

00:26:11.640 --> 00:26:13.080
You gave me money.

00:26:13.640 --> 00:26:15.080
You gave me power.

00:26:15.880 --> 00:26:19.560
Now I am successful, rich, and powerful.

00:26:20.120 --> 00:26:21.960
And that is the truth.

00:26:27.400 --> 00:26:28.680
Everybody was quiet.

00:26:29.720 --> 00:26:31.720
Then Inspector Sack took out his gun.

00:26:32.360 --> 00:26:33.800
Mrs. Seeker screamed.

00:26:34.440 --> 00:26:37.080
Inspector Sack shot Professor Verity.

00:26:37.880 --> 00:26:41.560
And Doctor Simple destroyed the truth machine.

00:26:49.560 --> 00:27:10.200
The truth machine was read by Stephen Pacey.

00:27:10.760 --> 00:27:15.480
And the recording produced by James Richardson at Studio AVP London.

00:27:17.560 --> 00:27:18.760
End of Side One.

00:27:19.560 --> 00:27:21.560
End of Side One.

